Z||000004||Raydar||05-06-2000||07:34 PM||||DXR, Mine does it, too. Digital cell phones will probably do it worse, because of the way the signal is transmitted. I'm surprised you hear it from other cars, though. <BR>Nextel and Southern LINC phones will probably *raise hell* through your stereo, if they are in close proximity.<BR>Try checking all the grounds, and make sure the antenna cable is plugged in tightly. Make sure all your shielded signal cables are plugged in tight, too.<BR>Does the loudness of the interference change when you turn the volume control down? If it does, then it's getting into the head unit. If not, it probably is going straight in to the EQ or amp. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||05-06-2000||07:57 PM||||You hear it all the time here. Over the radio, on tv, hell - sometimes even my fillings pick up the signal...||||reg||1
