Z||000007||DXR_DAD||05-07-2000||01:12 AM||||The volume does not effect the buzz at all.<BR>should I re-wire the whole system and check all grounds, I don't want to!! but........?<P>Terry I'll see if I can reach you. I'll be on KBLX 102.9FM   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||05-07-2000||09:45 AM||||DXR, I don't know how bad your interference is. I don't know that I would rewire everything, though. <BR>You said that you have a stock radio. I am assuming (there's that word) that you are using some sort of adapters to run your "speaker level" signal into your EQ, unless your EQ already has high level inputs. In any event, I'm guessing that you are using some sort of zip cord or speaker wire to connect between your head unit and EQ. You might try twisting those wires, for their entire length. Easist way to do that is to clamp one end of the wire in a vise, and clamp the other end in a drill. Pull back on the wire to give it a bit of tension, then let 'er fly. <BR>Note: there is absolutely no guarantees that this will work. This is a shot in the dark. The theory is that the twist will cause the interfering signal to be introduced into one conductor as much as the other and will, hopefully, cancel out. <BR>If the signal is getting in somewhere else, then this is a wasted effort. <BR>Fierosound, or anybody, please feel free to jump in!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||05-07-2000||10:00 AM||||My scanner picks them up all the time.  Very...um...interesting conversations. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||05-07-2000||10:18 AM||||Used to work for a company that installed car phones. (This was waaaayyy before cellular.) We maintained the towers that broadcasted to the car phones, as well. That being the case, we had to monitor the transmitters to make sure that they were operating within FCC specs, and such. <BR>One afternoon, we heard our top sales-person on her car phone. Suddenly, we realized how she got to be our top sales-person.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>(Not that it was a real surprise, or anything.)||||reg||1
Z||000011||ryshask||05-07-2000||04:12 PM||||It sounds like you have a nextel. Nextel are really crappy phones and their interference can be heard if your near any stereo equipment.||||reg||8
